VERDICT LOGIC:
 If brute b_k == Taylor c_k  => the Mayer cluster series IS log I, and the
    worker's 'b_2 = -|E|' is then a DIFFERENT object (NOT the log-I coeff).
 If brute b_k == worker's -|E| (i.e. != c_k) => the worker's b_k is the
    cluster integral but does NOT sum to log I; 'log I = sum b_k z^k' is wrong.
